<title>GERMANY: Bundesbank sets 15-day tender at fixed 3 pct.</title>
<headline>Bundesbank sets 15-day tender at fixed 3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank said on Tuesday it was setting a tender for 15-day securities repurchase funds, offering banks liquidity at a fixed rate of three percent.</p>
<p>Funds will be credited to accounts tomorrow and the securities have to be repurchased on January 2.</p>
<p>A 77 billion mark facility at a fixed three percent expires on Wednesday.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
